00:42:00,000 --> 00:42:06,000
Zombieland is a 2009 American post-apocalyptic zombie comedy film directed by Ruben
Fleischer, in his directorial debut, and written by Rhett Reese and Paul Wernick.

15
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
It stars Woody Harrelson, Jesse Eisenberg, Emma
Stone, Abigail Breslin and Bill Murray.

16
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
In the film, four survivors of a zombie apocalypse, Tallahassee (Harrelson), Columbus (Eisenberg), Wichita (Stone) and Little Rock (Breslin)
make their way on an extended cross-country road trip to find a sanctuary free from an evil virus that turns people into zombies.

17
00:51:00,000 --> 00:51:06,000
Development for Zombieland began in 2005, when Reese and Wernick
originally wrote the film as a spec script for a television pilot.

18
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:06,000
Fleischer helped develop the teleplay into a
screenplay for a self-contained feature.

19
00:57:00,000 --> 00:57:06,000
Tony Gardner was hired as the film's special effects makeup designer, which
primarily features physical prosthetics to create the look of the zombies.

20
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
Principal photography for the film began in February 2009 and lasted until that March, with
filming locations including Hollywood, Atlanta and in and around Georgia.

21
01:03:00,000 --> 01:03:06,000
Some of the film's scenes contained improvisation by the actors.

22
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:06,000
Zombieland premiered at Fantastic Fest on September 25, 2009, and was theatrically
released in the United States on October 2, by Sony Pictures Releasing.

23
01:09:00,000 --> 01:09:06,000
The film received positive critical reception, with praise for its
screenplay, dialogue, comedy, and cast performances.

24
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
It grossed $102 million worldwide, becoming the
tenth-highest grossing zombie film in the U.S.

25
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:06,000
until the release of World War Z (2013), and $54 million in home sales.

26
01:18:00,000 --> 01:18:06,000
A sequel, Zombieland: Double Tap, was released in October 2019.

27
